      <p><strong>Eccentricity:</strong> The concentration of 13,694 satellites (92.1%) in the 0.000–0.001 band confirms that virtually all active satellites maintain nearly circular orbits. The 32 satellites with eccentricity &gt; 0.5 are primarily Cold War-era payloads, Molniya communication satellites, and specialized science missions requiring high-apogee passes over particular geographic regions.</p>
